{"schemaVersion":2,"id":"practice-专项-source-998619a4108b","kind":"practice","title":"【未上传】综合检测卷(二)（试题word）（可作答题）","year":"专项","region":"资料","variant":"可作答资料","instructions":[{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"综合检测卷(二)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"100分钟 120分"}]},{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"第一部分　阅读(共两节,满分50分)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"第一节　(共15小题;每小题2.5分,满分37.5分)"}]}],"sections":[{"id":"section-legacy","title":"旧卷综合题型","instructions":[],"layout":"flow","groups":[{"id":"group-legacy","instructions":[],"stimulusBlocks":[{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"阅读下列短文,从每题所给的A、B、C、D四个选项中选出最佳选项。"}]},{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"A"}]},{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"Tricia Hurt, her husband Brian, and their son Brady were out enjoying a fishing adventure on Marsh-Miller Lake in Wisconsin when they found a baby bear in huge suffering. According to the locals in the area, the little bear had been running on land with a plastic tub on his head for three to four days, but he somehow got into the water, worsening his condition."}]},{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"The bear could be seen swimming in fear and shifting away from the family as they edged the boat closer. He was terrified, but the tub was quickly filled with water and he was in danger of drowning."}]},{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"“Go a little faster, Brady. Get in front of him,”Tricia instructed her son to drive the boat closer to the animal. Brian got close to the bear and tried to pull the tub out, but it had become too slippery. Brian lost his control, but he wasn't discouraged because the bear's ears had managed to come loose. That meant the plastic tub wasn't stuck and he just had to get closer."}]},{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"The rescue lasted about five minutes and they made several attempts before the tub finally came off. Brady made the boat circle around the bear and his father gave one last try that set the animal free. Once the tub came off, the bear was able to swim easily to the shore and catch a much-needed break."}]},{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"The family was extremely relieved as Tricia called out to the swimming animal, “Swim happily.”"}]},{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"“We were so excited! We did our good deed for the day. It felt good to help the poor bear. You don't like to see animals struggle,”Tricia later said in an interview."}]},{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"When the Hurts returned to their resort, everyone offered their gratitude. Tracy, a native, said, “No one else had been able to help the bear for several days as it struggled with the deadly tub on its head. We need more people like the Hurts!”"}]},{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"1.What happened to the bear?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"A.He was drowned in the lake."}]},{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"B.He was hurt by hunters."}]},{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"C.He got a tub on his head."}]},{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"D.He got trapped by the locals."}]}],"sharedOptions":[],"questions":[{"id":"q-1","displayNumber":1,"sourceQuestionNumber":1,"type":"single_choice","promptBlocks":[{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"What happened to the bear?"}]}],"placement":{"kind":"standalone"},"options":[{"id":"A","label":"A","blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"He was drowned in the lake."}]}]},{"id":"B","label":"B","blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"He was hurt by hunters."}]}]},{"id":"C","label":"C","blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"He got a tub on his head."}]}]},{"id":"D","label":"D","blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"He got trapped by the locals."}]}]}],"blanks":[],"answerSpec":{"availability":"answered","gradingMode":"auto","kind":"choice","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"normalization":{"unicodeNfkc":true,"trim":true,"collapseSpaces":true,"caseSensitive":false}},"explanationBlocks":[],"sourceRefs":[{"sourceDocumentId":"998619a4108bd023b87a180c11dd24db5a1896938e31904274f23f861db8ceac","relativePath":"其它/【未上传】综合检测卷(二)（试题word）.docx","sha256":"998619a4108bd023b87a180c11dd24db5a1896938e31904274f23f861db8ceac","locator":{},"extractionMethod":"docx-xml","confidence":0.96}],"reviewStatus":"approved","dedupeSignature":{"questionContentFingerprint":"8dd7a556d2a8e6a3980003df9efb1f3889c99e5caba67e6c08e904266bbc7fd1","answerVariantFingerprint":"fa550974c83ec0cc927374d27f88f3b43d825d8cf81f4b9d0e031843a594a843"}},{"id":"q-2","displayNumber":2,"sourceQuestionNumber":2,"type":"single_choice","promptBlocks":[{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"Who pulled out the tub?"}]}],"placement":{"kind":"standalone"},"options":[{"id":"A","label":"A","blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"Tracy."}]}]},{"id":"B","label":"B","blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"Tricia."}]}]},{"id":"C","label":"C","blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"Brady."}]}]},{"id":"D","label":"D","blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"Brian."}]}]}],"blanks":[],"answerSpec":{"availability":"answered","gradingMode":"auto","kind":"choice","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"normalization":{"unicodeNfkc":true,"trim":true,"collapseSpaces":true,"caseSensitive":false}},"explanationBlocks":[],"sourceRefs":[{"sourceDocumentId":"998619a4108bd023b87a180c11dd24db5a1896938e31904274f23f861db8ceac","relativePath":"其它/【未上传】综合检测卷(二)（试题word）.docx","sha256":"998619a4108bd023b87a180c11dd24db5a1896938e31904274f23f861db8ceac","locator":{},"extractionMethod":"docx-xml","confidence":0.96}],"reviewStatus":"approved","dedupeSignature":{"questionContentFingerprint":"f949851a0e6f22